      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "PROBLEM",
      "narration_text": "A QR code is a grid of tiny squares. Each one is a single bit: dark means one, light means zero. It was invented in Japan in nineteen ninety-four, to track car parts on a factory line, which is why it's called Quick Response.",
