    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "narration_text": "First your camera has to find it. Those three big squares in the corners are finder patterns. They tell the phone where the code is, and which way up it's turned, even at an angle. The dotted lines between them count out the grid, so the phone knows where every square sits.",
