    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "MECHANISM",
      "narration_text": "Then it reads the data, starting at the bottom-right corner and snaking up and down, two columns at a time. Every eight bits make a byte, and the bytes spell out the link. A mask pattern is flipped over the top, so there are no big blank patches to confuse the camera.",
